  "description": "Two identical stages (two parties and their pigeonhole racks). In A «Reciprocal commitments» each party holds a commitment (● and ◆, each printing its holder) and the two cross between them; in B «Unilateral promise» only A's commitment is supplied and it travels alone — no empty place is drawn for a second one. A comparison table lists every event with each scenario's supplied position; a Δ guide links the rows that differ. \"Reciprocal\" and \"unilateral\" are supplied configurations only: no winner, no deficiency, no legal effect is shown.",
